We are looking for a Senior Engineer to join one of our teams - Bluebeam.

Our dedicated Bluebeam team develops award-winning PDF solutions trusted by 4 million users in architecture, engineering, and construction. The team builds industry-standard software for project collaboration, document markup, and workflow automation, serving AEC professionals and government agencies worldwide.

YOUR DAILY CHALLENGES

Design and build shared libraries, SDKs, and internal modules that other engineering teams depend on;
Develop service templates and golden paths that embed best practices and speed up how product teams ship new services;
Build internal developer tooling — CLIs, scaffolding, automation — that removes friction from everyday engineering work;
Write production code primarily in Go, with secondary work in .NET/C#, applying strong software engineering fundamentals;
Use working knowledge of AWS, Terraform, and CI/CD to design abstractions that make cloud infrastructure easy and safe for other teams to consume;
Partner across engineering teams to drive adoption of shared tooling and standards — by making them genuinely useful, not by mandate;
Gather feedback from internal engineering "customers" and iterate on tools and libraries based on real usage.

OUR EXPECTATIONS

At least 6+ years of professional software development experience;
Several years of production Go experience, ideally including libraries or modules that other teams depend on;
Working experience with .NET/C# in production (primary experience in Go can be exchanged with .NET/C# if the candidate is otherwise a strong fit);
Demonstrated track record of building something for an internal engineering audience — a shared library, service template, internal platform, or CLI tool;
Working knowledge of AWS, Terraform, and CI/CD — enough to design good abstractions and understand what product teams need, without this being your core function;
Strong software design and engineering fundamentals, including experience with distributed systems and API design;
Comfortable working across teams and driving adoption of tools and standards through usefulness rather than authority;
Excellent communication and collaboration skills;
Excellent English proficiency (written and verbal);
Bachelor's degree in computer science studies ;
Fluent in English.

CONSIDERED A PLUS

Experience with containerization and Kubernetes from a consumer/integration perspective;
Familiarity with observability practices (structured logging, metrics, dashboards);
Background in platform or developer experience (DevEx) engineering;
Contributions to open-source libraries or developer tools;
Experience migrating teams from ad hoc setups to standardised templates or platforms.

WHAT YOU WILL GET

Build infrastructure and deployment systems that enable millions of construction professionals to advance the way the world is built;
Hybrid work model;
Access to conferences, training programs, and self-learning platforms;
Supportive environment where your ideas matter and technical excellence is valued;
Shape your role and grow within a 450+ person organisation with 25+ years of software excellence;
Diverse internal events and activities to build relationships across teams;
Comprehensive benefits and financial compensation.

We're looking for people with creative minds and enthusiasm to join us in developing what's new, what's next, and what best serves our customers' needs.
Ready to make an impact in software development? We'd be happy to welcome you to our team.

